FINDINGS -- Amdahl inverts on the GPU, exactly as the strategy doc predicted
  1. The A40 erases the O(N^2) compute: P7 117.2 -> 0.26 s (450x), A1
     16.6 -> 0.02 s. Wall clock is now ENTIRELY CPU/comm residue.
  2. Best end-to-end config on this node: mpi-gpu np8 = 36.2 s -- 4.6x vs
     cpu np1, 1.4x vs the previous best (mpi-cpu np8, 51.2 s). On a 1-GPU
     node the MPI ranks' whole contribution is decomposing the CPU-side
     phases (P3 27.3 -> 3.5 s incl. gather).
  3. np8 sharing one A40 costs: P7 0.26 -> 1.78 s (8 ranks' kernel launches
     + j-sends serialize on the device) and A1 0.02 -> 0.12 s (the C1
     gpupot_range fallback runs the FULL O(N^2) potential per rank -- the
     true ranged kernel is the G2 item, now measurable but tiny here).
  4. NEW RESIDUE RANKING (gpu np8): A2-A1 ADJUST bookkeeping 15.5 s >>
     OUTPUT 8.4 s >> P3 slice+gather 3.5 s > P2 2.5 s. The A2 growth vs
     np1 (8.8 -> 15.6 s) is the same replicated-sweep DRAM contention seen
     on mpi-cpu. ADJUST internals + OUTPUT are now 2/3 of the np8 wall.
  5. SURPRISE -- gpuirr library choice: the gpu/mpi-gpu variants link the
     hand-SSE gpuirr.sse.cpp (P3 np1 = 27.3 s); mpi-cpu links the scalar
     gpuirr.cpp which gcc -march=native auto-vectorizes (AVX-512 on this
     Xeon: P3 np1 = 9.1 s, 3x faster). RECOMMENDATION: try mpi-gpu with
     gpuirr.cpu.o (one Makefile line); at np8 it would cut P3+P3c from
     ~3.5 s toward ~1.5 s. Left unchanged in G0 (composition mirrors the
     shipped `gpu' variant 1:1); needs its own equiv re-run if adopted.

